{"id": "EUVD-2026-78808", "enisaUuid": "3d0117ee-701b-3450-813f-9ff9f4a3736e", "description": "FreeRDP versions before 3.31.0 contain an out-of-bounds write vulnerability in the urbdrc client channel's urb_send_current_frame_number_result() function. A malicious RDP server can send a crafted 28-byte USB redirection message to trigger a 4-byte write past the allocated 16-byte buffer, causing denial of service when verbose asserts are enabled.", "datePublished": "2026-09-15T15:18:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-20T00:35:29", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-h5w2-q35j-443h", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-3.14.0-through-3.30.0-out-of-bounds-write-via-urbdrc"], "aliases": ["GHSA-8rv4-fc8j-9xvc", "CVE-2026-91951"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.38, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ad445f7a-7da6-3ff9-af81-bebdbd85f9a3", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "3.14.0 <3.31.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "becd13a5-3ffe-3f79-9230-4f779dafce79", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}], "isExploited": false}